Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:45:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Files: the printer's card

Halyard copies each file to the printer's own SD card before the printer prints it. A new
panel under G-Code Files shows that card as Halyard last listed it (printer.card.list): the
8.3 names, the long names where the printer reports them, and which file in Halyard's
library each one came from, with a warning when the card's copy is not the one Halyard
wrote. Its other columns are G-Code Files' own, chosen and ordered by that panel's settings
and drawn by its cells and thumbnail: the card's size and date, and for a current copy the
metadata of the library file it came from (the printer can't send a file back, so other
files show "--"). A file can be printed as it is (M23, M24) or deleted (M30), after a
confirmation, and a selection deleted one file after another. A file the printer can't open
over serial (one in a folder, on Marlin 2.1.2 and older) comes with "locked": its row can't
be selected, printed or deleted, and a lock says why. Halyard lists the card only while the
printer is idle, so during a print the panel shows the last listing and says why, and its
buttons are off. It lists again when the halyard object's card_version changes, and on the
refresh button.

G-Code Files' context menu gets "Copy to the printer's card", a hand-off without a print
(printer.card.copy), whose progress shows in the status panel. Halyard's methods are typed
in types/moonraker/HalyardRPC.ts. Everything here shows only when the printer objects
include halyard.

